  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 445 PM MST Fri Nov 13 2026/ \n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nThis afternoon an upper-level ridge is moving eastward away from \nMontana with southerly flow aloft. Due to warm air advection there \nwill be well-above seasonal average temperatures across North-\ncentral, Central, and Southwestern Montana this afternoon. Due to \nmoist easterly winds flowing up the Milk River Valley through \ntomorrow morning, fog will linger in the Milk River Valley through \ntomorrow morning. See the Forecast Confidence & Scenarios Section \nfor details. On Saturday the southerly flow aloft remains over North-\ncentral, Central, and Southwestern Montana. A weak upper-level \nshortwave trough will move through the upper-level system. This will \nbring light rain and snow showers to Southwestern Montana during the \nday on Saturday. Across North-central, Central, and Southwestern \nMontana it will remain well-above seasonal averages for temperatures \non Saturday.\n\nOn Sunday an upper-level ridge builds in over North-central, \nCentral, and Southwestern Montana. This will keep warm (well-above \nseasonal average) temperatures and mostly dry weather for the area \non Sunday. On Monday the upper-level ridge remains over North-\ncentral, Central, and Southwestern Montana with strong southerly \nflow aloft. On Monday it will remain warm (well-above seasonal \naverages) and mostly dry. \n\nOn Tuesday an upper-level trough associated with a Pacific Cold \nFront will move over North-central, Central, and Southwestern \nMontana. This will bring cooler temperatures and widespread \nprecipitation to the area on Tuesday. Wednesday through Thursday \nthere will be upper-level troughing around. This will cool \ntemperatures down to below seasonal averages with precipitation \nchances. -IG\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nAcross the Milk River Valley in Hill and Blaine Counties there is a \n50 - 80% chance for dense fog to form. As a result a Dense Fog\nAdvisory is in effect for Hill County through 11 AM Saturday \nmorning and a Dense Fog Advisory goes into affect for Northern \nBlaine County from 9 PM tonight through 11 AM Saturday morning. \n\nFrom Monday night through Wednesday morning there is considerable\nuncertainty in how cold it gets and precipitation amounts. \nHowever there is high certainty that beginning Monday night into \nTuesday there will be a significant pattern change to colder and\nwetter weather. -IG",
